    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Strobo B M (Berlin/Munchen) is a Munich-based graphic design studio founded in Berlin in 2012 by Matthias Friederich and Julian von Klier, following an Olafur Eliasson scholarship and a teaching position at the Berlin University of the Arts. Relocated to Munich in 2014. The studio specialises in visual identities, editorial design, exhibition graphics, and web design for cultural and architectural institutions (Kunsthalle Bielefeld, Lenbachhaus, Architekturmuseum Pinakothek der Moderne, DETAIL magazine, KIT Karlsruhe). Five-person studio: two founding partners plus three collaborators (Sabrina Baumann, Monnier Ostermair, Luis Schneider). Multiple awards including German Design Award, Digital Emmy Award, Schonste Bucher Deutschlands, ADC, and 100 Beste Plakate. Studio-level autonomy: two founding creative directors running an independent practice since 2012; Autonomy set to 5 (fully autonomous, their own studio).",
      "source_url": null,
      "verified_at": "2026-07-06T01:05:30",
